meta-analysis.cz — licensing
============================

This file covers the material published at https://meta-analysis.cz.
Three different things are licensed differently. Please read the part that
applies to what you are using.


1. THE COLLECTION AND ITS DERIVED DATA LAYER
--------------------------------------------
Licence: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
         https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

This covers the compilation itself and everything generated from it:

  - the dataset index and API (`/api/v1/`), including `datasets.json`,
    the per-dataset codebooks, `datapackage.json` and the Croissant record
  - the Parquet and CSV mirrors under `/data/v1/<project>/`
  - the harmonised estimate-level table (`estimates_harmonised.*`)
  - the selection, arrangement and documentation of the collection

You may copy, redistribute, adapt and build upon this material, including
commercially, provided you give appropriate credit.

Cite the collection as:

  Havránek, T. and Z. Iršová (2026). meta-analysis.cz: data and code for
  meta-analyses in economics. https://meta-analysis.cz


2. THE UNDERLYING RESEARCH DATASETS
------------------------------------
Each dataset under `/data/v1/<project>/` and each original file in a project
folder was assembled for a specific published paper, with its own authors and
co-authors. Those datasets remain the work of their respective author teams.

The compilation licence in section 1 is granted by the maintainers of this site
over the collection they assembled. It is not a re-licensing of any co-author's
independent rights in an underlying dataset, and it does not override any terms
attached to a dataset by its publisher or by a third-party data provider.

**If you use an individual dataset, cite its paper.** Every dataset entry in
`/api/v1/datasets.json` carries the paper's title, authors and DOI for exactly
this purpose. This is the normal scholarly expectation and, for most of these
datasets, also the condition on which the underlying material was shared.

Where a dataset was compiled from a third-party source with its own terms, the
codebook for that dataset records it. Two collections distributed here are not
extracted-estimate datasets and are not part of the harmonised layer: the
crisis database under `ews/` and the cross-field archive bundled in the MAIVE
replication package under `maive/`. Their original terms apply.


